/P 47 0 R
/E (At about 3:30 pm ET on 13 November, the FAA's legacy network was unstable, disrupting radar feeds and aircraft communications. A nationwide ground stop followed. About 3,500 aircraft in the air landed safely, and controllers kept some frequencies and radar feeds throughout.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [37]
>>
endobj
310 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 47 0 R
/E (The FAA says data flooded its network at roughly 1,000 connection attempts every four to five seconds. Early findings point to a radar set in Amarillo, Texas and a radio site in El Dorado, Arkansas, where provider L3Harris had been fitting a new router. Both sites were blocked and the network settled.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [38]
>>
endobj
